From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/37] ec/lenovo/h8: Let mainboards put the H8 options in
 their own forms

The H8 setup options are always in four generic forms (Power, Devices,
Keyboard/Mouse, Other), which come after the forms of the mainboard. A
mainboard that groups its setup menu differently, for example keyboard
options next to its own, has no way to use them.

Make the option objects global, with an h8_cfr_ prefix and declared in
ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h, and add H8_CFR_MAINBOARD_FORMS: when a mainboard
selects it, the generic forms are left out and the mainboard lists the
objects in its own forms. Nothing selects it yet, so the menu does not
change.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
